    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Description\n\nA very nice feature would be to have line blame, maybe as virtual text, very much line gitsigns.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI did think about adding it. Not as a part of 'mini.diff', but as something like `MiniGit.toggle_line_blame()` (probably needs a better name since I don't really like the \"blame\" part, although it is canonical) in 'mini.git' which acts similarly to `MiniDiff.toggle_overlay()`.\n\nBut it is not high priority. Mostly since there is `:Git blame` with [possibly adjusted output](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-git.html#minigit-examples-tweakingcommandoutput).",
